2b:["$","div","b6392",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can I trim and split videos on Melius?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. The multi-track editor supports trimming clip boundaries and splitting clips, so you can keep the useful section of a take and arrange it within a larger sequence."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can I combine video, text and audio?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. The timeline supports multiple tracks for assembling footage with still images, text and audio. Clip controls let you adjust the components of the cut separately."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can I change a clip's speed?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. The editor has playback-speed controls, with pitch-preserving audio handling. Changing speed affects the clip's timing, so review the surrounding sequence afterwards."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Which video file types can I export?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The verified Stitch output is MP4. Multiple video export types are not established by this workflow; a different delivery format requires a separate supported conversion step."}]]}]]}]
2c:["$","p","b6397",{"children":["Take three clips into ",["$","$L3b","b6395",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b6394","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":false},"children":["Melius"]}],". Cut them into one sequence before generating a fourth."]}]
2e:["$","$L2d","post-product-hero-shot",{"post":{"_key":"post-product-hero-shot","slug":"product-hero-shot","category":"guides","title":"How to generate a product hero shot on Melius","metaTitle":"How to make product photos with AI: the hero shot","isoDate":"2026-09-14","date":"September 14, 2026","readTime":"7 Min Read","excerpt":"Generate a product hero shot from a pack shot on Melius, and keep the product dimensionally and visually accurate instead of nearly right.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/product-hero-shot/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"Can I use AI for product photography?","answer":"Yes, for hero shots, lifestyle scenes, background variants and channel-specific crops, generated from a pack shot you already have. What it does not do on its own is guarantee the product is accurate, which is why the workflow feeds in the product's real specifications and branding as separate inputs and ends with a check against the actual item."},{"question":"What is a product hero shot?","answer":"The main image a shopper sees first, on a listing, an ad or a landing page. It has to read at a glance and it has to look like the thing that arrives, which is why it's the shot where product fidelity matters most."},{"question":"Why does my logo come out wrong in AI product photos?","answer":"Because the model draws your logo from scratch on every generation. It rebuilds an approximation of everything in frame, and a logo is exactly the kind of arbitrary artwork that can't be inferred from context. Adding the logo file as its own reference node, and instructing the prompt not to redraw it, is the fix."},{"question":"Do I still need a photographer?","answer":"For the input, often yes. This workflow starts from a clean pack shot, and the quality of that photograph sets the ceiling on everything generated from it. What changes is the volume: one good pack shot can carry a season of scenes, ratios and variants that would each have been a separate setup."},{"question":"How do I keep a product consistent across many shots?","answer":"Build the canvas once on a single SKU until the output is right, then duplicate it and swap the inputs. Reusing the graph is what keeps the lighting and the framing from drifting between shots, and it's how high-volume teams produce variants at catalogue scale."},{"question":"What resolution should I generate product shots at?","answer":"2K or higher. Generating at 2K isn't the same as upscaling a 1K image afterwards: the model has more room to resolve fabric weave, embossed marks and label typography while it works, and upscaling later operates on an image whose fine detail is already gone. Note that the canvas preview is downscaled at any resolution, so judge sharpness from the full-screen view or the download."},{"question":"How much does generating product photos cost?","answer":"Generation runs on credits from one shared pool, whichever model a step uses, so trying the same shot on two models costs nothing extra in setup. Current plans and credit allowances are on the pricing page."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"key-takeaways","title":"Key takeaways"},{"_key":"product-hero-shots-from-a-pack-shot","title":"Product hero shots from a pack shot"},{"_key":"why-generated-products-come-back-nearly-right","title":"Why generated products come back nearly right"},{"_key":"building-the-shot-step-by-step","title":"Building the shot, step by step"},{"_key":"where-product-shots-go-wrong","title":"Where product shots go wrong"},{"_key":"scaling-one-shot-across-a-catalogue","title":"Scaling one shot across a catalogue"},{"_key":"why-this-runs-the-way-it-does-on-melius","title":"Why this runs the way it does on Melius"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b6032","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6031","text":"Key takeaways","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"key-takeaways"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6034","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6033","text":"A hero shot needs three separate inputs, not one prompt. A clean product shot, your product's real specifications, and a style reference each go in as their own node, and the prompt's job is mostly to say what must not change.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6036","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6035","text":"Branding is the part the model invents. An image model regenerates a logo rather than placing your logo file, so the mark comes back nearly right and specifically wrong. Give it the artwork as its own input and tell it not to redraw it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6038","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6037","text":"A lifestyle photo is not a product reference. The model needs a clean, evenly lit view of the product itself. Mood references and product references do different jobs and go in separately.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6040","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6039","text":"Generate at 2K or higher, not 1K. Fine detail is where fidelity is won or lost: fabric weave, embossing, label type. More resolution gives the model more to work with on exactly those features.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6042","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6041","text":"Correct on the node, don't start over. When scale or placement is off, edit that node's prompt with the specific fix and re-run it. Re-prompting the whole canvas throws away the parts that worked.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6044","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6043","text":"Product hero shots from a pack shot","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"product-hero-shots-from-a-pack-shot"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6046","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6045","text":"To generate a product hero shot on Melius, put a clean pack shot of the product on the canvas, add its real specifications and a style reference as separate inputs, connect all three into an image-to-image node at 2K, and write a prompt that names the scene while stating plainly that the product itself must not change. Then run three or four variations and inspect them full screen.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6048","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6047","text":"The workflow is easy. Getting the product to look like your product is the part that takes practice, and it's the complaint marketers raise most often on onboarding calls. The shot is beautiful and the proportions are subtly off, or the logo resembles your logo, or the fabric drapes like a stock photo rather than like the thing you sell. Nearly all of that traces to one cause, and it's fixable.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6050","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6049","text":"Why generated products come back nearly right","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-generated-products-come-back-nearly-right"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6052","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6051","text":"An image model doesn't paste your product into a scene. Whatever falls inside the region it generates gets rebuilt as an approximation from what it can infer, so anything it can't infer gets invented. Your logo isn't a shape it can reason its way to, real proportions aren't recoverable from one photograph, and the weight and fall of your material isn't something a prompt adjective conveys.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6054","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6053","text":"What fixes it is giving the model your actual assets as distinct inputs, then being explicit about which of them are fixed. Prompt wording alone won't get you there. Every step below removes one more thing from the set the model is guessing at.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6056","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6055","text":"Building the shot, step by step","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"building-the-shot-step-by-step"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6061","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6058","href":"https://docs.melius.com/help-center/marketers/recipes/product-swap","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6057","text":"The click path is in the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6059","text":"help centre recipe for product photos and swaps","marks":["b6058"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6060","text":". The shape of the work is this:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6063","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6062","text":"Drop your pack shot on the canvas. A clean product photo on a neutral background. If you have several angles, bring them all in and unified-group them, so the agent works from every angle rather than one.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6065","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6064","text":"Give the agent the real specifications. Ask it in chat to pull dimensions, materials and colour from your product page URL and save them as a text node. It now has your stated specs to work from rather than inferring everything from a photograph.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6067","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6066","text":"Add the logo as its own node. If the product carries visible branding, put the logo file on the canvas separately and connect it in. In the prompt, tell the model to use that reference exactly and not to redraw it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6069","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6068","text":"Add a style reference for the look. A moodboard or a past campaign, turned into a style description. It governs light, composition and mood, and stays separate from everything describing the product.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6071","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6070","text":"Create an image-to-image node at 2K. Melius recommends Nano Banana Pro for material and lighting fidelity, and GPT Image 2 (High) where packaging text has to be legible (guidance current as of September 2026). Set the ratio you're shipping, and go 2K or 4K rather than 1K: the small features are the ones that give a shot away.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6073","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6072","text":"Wire the inputs to their jobs. Pack shot into the image input. Specifications, style description and logo into context. Then reference them by name in the prompt with @ mentions so the model knows which input governs what.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6075","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6074","text":"Write the prompt around what stays fixed. Name the scene in one line, then spend the rest on constraints: use the exact product from the reference, don't restyle it, don't change its colour, don't modify its shape or proportions.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6077","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6076","text":"Run three or four variations and inspect them full screen. The canvas preview is downscaled, and downscaling hides precisely the defects you're checking for. Open each candidate properly before you pick one.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6079","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6078","text":"Check the output against the actual item. Shape, colour, logo, any packaging text, proportions. A clean pack shot and real specs improve your odds; they do not remove the review step.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6081","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6080","text":"Where product shots go wrong","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-product-shots-go-wrong"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6083","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6082","text":"A lifestyle photo was used as the product reference. The product is small, partly hidden and lit for mood, so the model never gets a clean look at it. Add a studio shot or a transparent PNG as a separate product input.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6085","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6084","text":"No specifications went in. Dimensions and materials get inferred from a single image, and the model has no way to know how big the thing is or what it's made of.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6087","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6086","text":"The logo was left to the model. Branding is the one element where close enough is still wrong, because anyone who knows the brand knows what the mark should look like. It needs to be an input, not an output.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6089","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6088","text":"The whole thing got re-prompted over one flaw. When the product is 20% too small or facing the wrong way, that's a one-clause correction on the existing node, not a fresh start.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6094","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6091","href":"https://docs.melius.com/help-center/marketers/picking-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6090","text":"Typography and material were asked of one model. Rendering legible packaging copy and rendering convincing material are different problems, and a canvas can use a different model at each step. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6092","text":"Our per-job model guidance","marks":["b6091"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6093","text":" is in the help centre, and it changes as models ship.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6096","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6095","text":"Scaling one shot across a catalogue","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"scaling-one-shot-across-a-catalogue"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6098","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6097","text":"Once a canvas produces a shot you'd ship, the graph is the asset. Duplicate it, swap the pack shot and the specifications for the next SKU, and the light, composition and constraints carry over. That's how a team working through a catalogue gets consistency instead of forty shots that each look slightly different.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6100","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6099","text":"The neighbouring jobs start from the same graph: background variants for seasonal scenes, a swap to drop your product into a scene you already have, re-composition for each channel's ratio. Melius ships a Product Swapper preset for the swap once it becomes routine.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6102","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6101","text":"Why this runs the way it does on Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-this-runs-the-way-it-does-on-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6104","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6103","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, built on a node-based canvas where each input and output is a node and edges pass one node's result into the next. That structure is what makes product fidelity tractable: the pack shot, the specifications, the logo and the style are four things the graph holds separately, so you change one without disturbing the other three and re-run everything downstream.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6106","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6105","text":"You brief an agent in plain language and it wires the graph and runs the models. Every step stays open, so the prompt behind a nearly-right shot is right there to correct. You direct; the agent produces.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6108","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6107","text":"The models are on one subscription. Melius spans a library of leading models for image, video and audio, and agents route each step to the strongest one for that step unless you choose per node.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6110","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6109","text":"You own the content you create on Melius and can use, publish, and distribute it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms. Melius doesn't claim ownership of your work and doesn't use it to train AI models.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6118","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6112","href":"/blog/static-ad-from-style-reference","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b6115","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6111","text":"For related workflows, see ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6113","text":"building a static ad from a style reference","marks":["b6112"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6114","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6116","text":"choosing a Nano Banana model","marks":["b6115"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6117","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6120","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6119","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b6121","items":"$2e:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6126","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6123","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6122","text":"Have a pack shot and a product page? ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6124","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b6123"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6125","text":" and build the canvas on one SKU first.","marks":[]}]}]}}]
2f:["$","$L2d","post-ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared",{"post":{"_key":"post-ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared","slug":"ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared","category":"comparisons","title":"AI video generators for filmmakers, compared","isoDate":"2026-09-14","date":"September 14, 2026","readTime":"22 Min Read","excerpt":"Eight tools compared on what a director actually needs: shot control, consistency across cuts, an editorial surface, and whether the footage clears.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best AI video generator for filmmakers?","answer":"There isn't one, and the honest answer depends on which constraint binds. Runway has the best edit surface, Luma the best color and finishing, Kling the best per-shot camera control, Google Flow the best dialogue and coverage, and Moonvalley Marey and Adobe Firefly both emphasize licensed training data for commercial work. Melius combines access to leading models with image, video and audio uploads and an in-app multi-track editor, so generation and assembly can happen in one workflow."},{"question":"Can you use AI-generated video in a film festival entry?","answer":"It depends on the festival, and the rules are mostly about disclosure rather than prohibition. The Academy's 99th Oscars rules require acting roles to be credited in the legal billing and demonstrably performed by humans with their consent, and screenplays to be human-authored, which closes those two categories to AI while leaving the rest of the ballot open. The same rules say generative AI tools neither help nor harm the chances of a nomination, with each branch judging the degree to which a human was at the heart of the creative authorship. Sundance, SXSW and Tribeca lean on disclosure. Cannes publishes no AI provision in its 2026 feature-film regulations at all, so check the specific festival's current rules before you submit."},{"question":"Is Sora still available?","answer":"No. OpenAI discontinued the Sora web and app experiences on 26 April 2026, and its own help centre states the Sora API will be discontinued on 24 September 2026. OpenAI has not announced a successor video model. Several roundups and a few platforms still list Sora 2 as available, so treat any current recommendation of it as out of date."},{"question":"How long can AI-generated video clips be?","answer":"Native single-shot length runs from a few seconds to 30 depending on the model, and that number matters more than any advertised maximum. Veo 3.1 does 8 seconds, Gemini Omni Flash 10, Kling 3.0 up to 15, Luma's Ray3.2 offers 5 or 10 seconds for text-to-video and image-to-video, or up to 20 seconds when modifying existing video, and Seedance 2.5 up to 30 in a single generation. Anything longer is stitched, and stitching is where faces, wardrobe and lighting start to drift."},{"question":"Do you own the rights to AI-generated footage?","answer":"Usually yes on a paid plan, but the terms differ enough that they need checking per tool before anything is delivered. On Melius, you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Elsewhere the variation is real: Runway trains on your inputs and outputs on every plan below Enterprise, Luma requires an active paid subscription at the moment of generation for commercial rights to vest, and free tiers across the category generally grant the provider far broader rights than paid ones."},{"question":"Which AI video model is the highest quality right now?","answer":"On blind preference testing, Alibaba's Wan 3.0 and Google's Gemini Omni Flash are tied at the top, followed by MiniMax H3 Max and then the Seedance 2.0 entry. The uncomfortable part for a filmmaker is that the top of that board is almost entirely models with restricted, unclear or litigated Western commercial terms, and that neither Runway's Gen-4.5 nor any Luma model appears anywhere on the with-audio board at all, despite being the two most production-ready tools here. Quality rankings and usability rankings are not the same list."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"which-ai-video-generator-should-a-filmmaker-use","title":"Which AI video generator should a filmmaker use?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-tool-for-film-work","title":"What separates a good tool for film work?"},{"_key":"the-eight-compared","title":"The eight compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-runway","title":"2. Runway"},{"_key":"3-google-flow","title":"3. Google Flow"},{"_key":"4-luma","title":"4. Luma"},{"_key":"5-kling","title":"5. Kling"},{"_key":"6-moonvalley-marey","title":"6. Moonvalley Marey"},{"_key":"7-ltx-studio","title":"7. LTX Studio"},{"_key":"8-adobe","title":"8. Adobe"},{"_key":"what-still-needs-a-camera","title":"What still needs a camera"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5575","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5574","text":"Which AI video generator should a filmmaker use?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"which-ai-video-generator-should-a-filmmaker-use"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5577","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5576","text":"Decide first whether the footage has to clear, because that single question splits this category in two and the split has nothing to do with output quality. If the work is going to a client, a festival or a distributor, provenance and rights govern, and the models at the top of the quality leaderboards are mostly the ones you can't use. If it's a test, a pitch piece or a look-development pass, pick on control and ignore the paperwork.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5579","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5578","text":"The second thing to settle is where the cut happens. Some of these tools generate and hand you files. Some now generate inside a timeline. That difference decides whether you're editing a film or reconciling a folder of clips, and it matters more day to day than any spec on the model card.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5581","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5580","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5583","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5582","text":"Native shot length is the spec that matters, not maximum length. Stitching is where faces drift, wardrobe shifts and lighting rolls, so a tool that gives you 20 seconds in one take beats one that reaches 20 by joining four.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5585","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5584","text":"For the 99th Oscars the Academy requires acting roles to be credited in the film's legal billing and demonstrably performed by humans with their consent, and screenplays to be human-authored. That closes the acting and writing categories to AI and leaves the rest of the ballot open.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5587","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5586","text":"Check who trains on your material. Runway trains on inputs and outputs by default on every plan below Enterprise, and free tiers across this category generally grant much broader rights than paid ones.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5589","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5588","text":"Test the second and third shot, never the first. Identity drift across a sequence ruins a scene faster than any single clip's quality, and it doesn't show up in a demo reel.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5591","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5590","text":"What separates a good tool for film work?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-tool-for-film-work"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5593","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5592","text":"Four criteria, and the last one eliminates most of the current quality leaders for anything that has to be delivered.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5595","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5594","text":"It's directable, not promptable","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5597","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5596","text":"A prompt describes a vibe. A shot list describes a lens, a height, a move and a duration. The tools worth a director's time let you specify those separately from the content, so you can keep the scene and change the coverage.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5599","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5598","text":"The gap here is wide. Kling's Video 3.0 Omni takes duration, shot size, perspective and camera movement per shot in a custom multi-shot plan. Seedance 2.5 accepts 3D camera blockouts, which is the closest thing in the category to actual blocking. Most other tools offer a preset menu and hope.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5601","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5600","text":"The character survives the cut","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5603","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5602","text":"Consistency inside one clip is a solved problem. Consistency across a scene isn't, and it's the thing that separates footage you can edit from footage you can only post. Look for reference systems that persist: multiple reference images, character nodes, first and last frame conditioning, or a conversational context that holds a face and a wardrobe across successive generations.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5605","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5604","text":"The honest test is a shot-reverse-shot. Generate a wide, then a matching close, then go back to the wide. If the jacket changed, the tool cannot cut a scene yet.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5607","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5606","text":"It lands in a timeline","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5609","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5608","text":"2026 is the year this stopped being a nice-to-have. Adobe put generative models inside the Premiere timeline in September, Runway built a purpose-built edit surface around its editing model, and LTX Studio ships a script-to-shot-sequence front end. Melius also includes an in-app multi-track editor, so you can generate shots, arrange them and layer audio in one workspace. Tools without an editing surface still ask you to export, import and reconcile.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5611","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5610","text":"The round trip isn't a small tax. It's where versions multiply, where a re-generated shot loses its place in the cut, and where most of the time on an AI-assisted project actually goes.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5613","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5612","text":"The footage clears","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5615","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5614","text":"Two models in this comparison are trained only on material their makers licensed: Moonvalley's Marey, built largely on B-roll that filmmakers and agencies deliberately licensed plus archive partnerships, and Adobe's Firefly, trained on licensed Adobe Stock and public domain content and never on customer work. Everything else carries some degree of open question.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5617","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5616","text":"The question isn't academic in 2026. Disney and Paramount Skydance sent cease-and-desist letters to ByteDance over Seedance 2.0, MiniMax is in active copyright litigation brought by Disney, Universal and Warner Bros. Discovery, and its open-weights license excludes the US, UK, EU and South Korea by default, and Alibaba's Wan 3.0 is API-only and closed-weight, with no published weights or license text at all. A legal department will clear Marey and Firefly. It'll ask hard questions about the rest.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5619","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5618","text":"The eight compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-eight-compared"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5621","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5620","text":"Capabilities as of September 2026, from each tool's own documentation, model cards and pricing pages. No scores: which shot looks better is a judgment call, so every column here is something you can verify.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b5622","rows":[{"_key":"b5623","cells":[{"_key":"b5624","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5626","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5625","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b5627","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5629","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5628","text":"Best at","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b5630","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5632","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5631","text":"Native single shot","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b5633","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5635","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5634","text":"Editorial surface","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b5636","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5638","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5637","text":"Clearance posture","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5639","cells":[{"_key":"b5640","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5642","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5641","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5643","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5645","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5644","text":"Reaching every leading video model in one workflow","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5646","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5648","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5647","text":"Depends on the model you route to","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5649","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5651","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5650","text":"In-app multi-track editor, plus canvas-based workflows","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5652","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5654","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5653","text":"You own the output, subject to each model provider's terms","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5655","cells":[{"_key":"b5656","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5658","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5657","text":"Runway","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5659","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5661","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5660","text":"Propagating an edit across a multi-shot sequence","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5662","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5664","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5663","text":"2 to 10 seconds on Gen-4.5","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5665","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5667","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5666","text":"Edit Studio, plus Premiere and After Effects plugins","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5668","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5670","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5669","text":"Trains on your work on every plan below Enterprise","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5671","cells":[{"_key":"b5672","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5674","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5673","text":"Google Flow","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5675","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5677","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5676","text":"Coverage with native synchronized dialogue","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5678","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5680","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5679","text":"4, 6 or 8 seconds on Veo 3.1, 10 on Gemini Omni Flash","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5681","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5683","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5682","text":"Flow canvas and Scenebuilder","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5684","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5686","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5685","text":"SynthID on every output, visible watermark is a toggle","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5687","cells":[{"_key":"b5688","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5690","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5689","text":"Luma","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5691","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5693","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5692","text":"Color and finishing that survive a real grade","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5694","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5696","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5695","text":"5 or 10 seconds; up to 20 in video-to-video","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5697","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5699","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5698","text":"None, it exports to yours","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5700","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5702","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5701","text":"You retain outputs, commercial use needs a paid plan","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5703","cells":[{"_key":"b5704","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5706","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5705","text":"Kling","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5707","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5709","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5708","text":"Per-shot camera direction and blocking","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5710","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5712","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5711","text":"3 to 15 seconds on Video 3.0","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5713","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5715","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5714","text":"None","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5716","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5718","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5717","text":"Terms expect outputs marked as AI generated","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5719","cells":[{"_key":"b5720","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5722","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5721","text":"Moonvalley Marey","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5723","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5725","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5724","text":"Footage a legal department will clear","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5726","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5728","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5727","text":"5 or 10 seconds via its inference partner","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5729","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5731","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5730","text":"None, built for your pipeline","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5732","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5734","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5733","text":"Trained only on owned and licensed data","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5735","cells":[{"_key":"b5736","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5738","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5737","text":"LTX Studio","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5739","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5741","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5740","text":"Pre-production structure, and open weights","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5742","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5744","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5743","text":"Multishot in one pass, auto duration","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5745","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5747","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5746","text":"Script to shot sequence, plus an edit suite","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5748","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5750","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5749","text":"Open-weights license with a revenue threshold","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b5751","cells":[{"_key":"b5752","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5754","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5753","text":"Adobe","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5755","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5757","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5756","text":"Generating without leaving the cut","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5758","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5760","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5759","text":"2 seconds of Generative Extend","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5761","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5763","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5762","text":"Premiere Pro and After Effects","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b5764","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5766","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5765","text":"Firefly is licensed-only, partner models are not","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5768","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5767","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5770","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5769","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work: you describe what you want and an agent builds the workflow, routes each step to a model and leaves every step open for you to change. A node-based canvas sits underneath, so a sequence is a graph you can inspect, branch and re-run, not a queue of unrelated jobs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5772","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5771","text":"For film work the argument is reach. One subscription puts Veo 3.1, Kling 3, Wan 3.0 and the Seedance family on the same canvas, alongside the rest of the library of leading models and the lipsync and avatar models. That matters because no single video model currently wins on shot control, audio, duration and grade at once, and the alternative to routing between them is eight subscriptions and eight interfaces.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5774","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5773","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5776","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5775","text":"Upload images, video and audio to the shared asset library and canvas, so a project can start with existing footage as well as generated material.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5778","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5777","text":"Per-step model routing, so the model that carries the motion isn't the one asked to hold a face, and the choice is per node, not per project.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5780","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5779","text":"Branching, which is the natural shape of comparing two directions on the same shot without rebuilding anything.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5782","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5781","text":"A Storyboard template turns a single image into a nine-panel sequence, which is a fast way to agree coverage before you spend on generation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5784","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5783","text":"Reference and character nodes carry one look across every clip in a set, and changing an upstream node re-runs everything below it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5786","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5785","text":"Every canvas is real-time and collaborative by default, so a director and a producer work in one place instead of trading exports.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5788","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5787","text":"It's drivable from Slack, a command line, an API and the Model Context Protocol (MCP), so a look-development pass can run from wherever the rest of the team already works.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5790","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5789","text":"Melius includes video editing and an in-app multi-track editor for arranging shots, timing and layering audio. Stitch nodes are another way to assemble clips on the canvas, not the only way to edit. You can work with generated shots and uploaded footage in the same workspace.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5792","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5791","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5794","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5793","text":"The trade-off is at the model level: supported references, native shot lengths, audio generation and output formats vary by the model you select. A shared workspace does not make those capabilities identical, so choose the model for each shot's requirements.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5796","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5795","text":"The catch: one workspace brings generation, assets and editing together, but each model still has its own capabilities and terms.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5798","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5797","text":"Best for: directors and small teams who want look development, previz, shot exploration and multi-track editing in one place, with a visible, re-runnable process and support for existing footage.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5803","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5800","href":"/pricing","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5799","text":"See ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5801","text":"Melius pricing","marks":["b5800"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5802","text":" for current plans and allowances.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5805","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5804","text":"2. Runway","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-runway"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5807","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5806","text":"Runway is the closest thing this category has to an industry standard, and in 2026 it has become the most editorially serious of the pure-plays. Aleph 2.0 and Edit Studio, both shipped on 21 May, give you a real edit surface where an instruction propagates across cuts in a multi-shot sequence rather than applying to one clip. Ruby, added in late August, is a Runway-native color grading model that takes an SDR input and produces true HDR.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5809","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5808","text":"September brought Runway plugins for Premiere Pro and After Effects, which puts its whole lineup inside the applications editors already live in. It also now hosts third-party models, including Wan 3.0 and Seedance 2.5 at 1080p, which is the cleanest route a US filmmaker has to either.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5811","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5810","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5813","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5812","text":"Edit Studio takes an input video between 2 and 30 seconds at up to 1080p with no more than ten cuts, and Aleph 2.0 applies your edit across the relevant shots.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5815","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5814","text":"Runway builds its own frontier models and ships them continuously: Aleph 2.0 and Ruby this summer, then Solaris and GWM Worlds 2 within four days of each other in late August and early September.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5817","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5816","text":"Genuine camera and motion control that assumes you know what a camera does.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5819","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5818","text":"The Adobe plugins remove the round trip for anyone cutting in Premiere.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5821","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5820","text":"Long-established use in professional film and advertising, so craft knowledge and tutorials are easy to find.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5823","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5822","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5825","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5824","text":"Two problems, and the first is uncomfortable. Runway's terms of use say inputs and outputs may be used to train and improve its models, and that applies to every plan except Enterprise, which is where you get no training on your data plus uncapped IP indemnification. For a director working on unreleased material that's a real objection, not a technicality.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5827","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5826","text":"The second is the credit budget. Runway meters generation by model and duration, so compare the current plan allowance with the shots and revisions you expect to produce. Gen-4.5 also sits outside the top ten on the blind preference boards, so you are paying for the surface around the model more than for the model.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5829","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5828","text":"The catch: the best edit surface in the category, on a model that no longer tops the rankings.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5831","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5830","text":"Best for: editors and directors who want generation and assembly in one place and are cutting in Premiere anyway.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5833","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5832","text":"3. Google Flow","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-google-flow"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5835","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5834","text":"Flow is Google's filmmaking front end, and it's the strongest all-rounder here for narrative coverage. Veo 3.1 produces 4, 6 or 8 second clips at 1080p and 4K, with 8 seconds available at those resolutions or when you pass reference images, and it generates native synchronized audio covering dialogue, effects and ambience in the same pass.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5837","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5836","text":"Gemini Omni Flash, announced in May, is the more interesting half. It's any-to-any, generates with native audio, and holds a character consistent across cuts through multi-turn editing, where Google's own framing is that the physics hold up and the scene remembers what came before. So you refine by talking about it instead of re-uploading references each time. Voice editing is not part of it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5839","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5838","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5841","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5840","text":"Native synchronized dialogue with accurate lip movement, which removes a whole ADR-shaped problem.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5843","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5842","text":"Ingredients to Video takes multiple reference images controlling character, object and style at once.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5845","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5844","text":"Frames to Video gives you start and end image control, and Extend runs a sequence past a minute.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5847","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5846","text":"Video-to-video editing, Characters and Avatars round out the surface, so a fix does not always mean a fresh generation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5849","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5848","text":"Gemini Omni Flash sits at the top of the blind text-to-video rankings, so the quality is not a compromise.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5851","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5850","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5853","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5852","text":"The clip ceiling is 8 seconds on Veo and 10 on Omni, which is short enough to shape how you write. Every Flow output also carries an invisible SynthID watermark, detectable programmatically rather than visible to a viewer. The visible watermark is a separate thing and it is worth getting right: it's a toggle in your own profile menu, not a paid-tier perk, and Flow applies it automatically only if you're in India, South Korea or Vietnam.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5855","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5854","text":"Google's commercial-rights language is also notably hard to locate for a product being sold to professionals, and Flow's own community forum carries unanswered questions about it. Note too that Flow is an individual Google AI subscription with no team tier, so a second person on the project means a second subscription.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5857","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5856","text":"The catch: the best all-round output, and the shortest shots.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5859","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5858","text":"Best for: directors who need dialogue and coverage more than long takes, and who can absorb the top tier.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5861","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5860","text":"4. Luma","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-luma"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5863","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5862","text":"Luma's Ray3.2, out in June, has the best finishing story in the category by a distance, and it's the only entry here that a colorist would recognize as pipeline-ready. It generates in native 16-bit color and exports 16-bit EXR frames in ACES2065-1, which drop straight into a grade and a comp without a conversion step.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5865","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5864","text":"It also gives the most granular in-clip pacing control available: Multi-Keyframe sets up to 16 keyframes inside a single clip, and performance tracking follows the full expressive state of up to eight faces frame by frame, with motion transfer and camera motion transfer alongside it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5867","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5866","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5869","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5868","text":"Resolutions from 360p to 1080p, with Modify Video reaching up to 20 seconds at 24fps and Reframe handling sources up to 16 seconds.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5871","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5870","text":"EXR output in ACES2065-1 and native 16-bit color, so the footage behaves like footage in a grade, and HDR works in video-to-video too.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5873","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5872","text":"16 keyframes per clip for real control over beats inside a shot.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5875","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5874","text":"Performance tracking across eight faces, and Modify Video preserves lip sync and dialogue timing when face tracking is on.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5877","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5876","text":"Ray3.2 was developed with working creatives from film, advertising and games, and ships an API aimed at studio pipelines.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5879","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5878","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5881","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5880","text":"No native audio on text-to-video or image-to-video. Luma's own FAQ is blunt about it: voiceover, music and sound effects are a separate step. Modify Video and Reframe preserve audio that already exists, but Luma will not generate a soundtrack, so anything with dialogue needs a second tool. The bigger constraint is length. Text-to-video and image-to-video produce 5-second or 10-second native clips, and the 20-second figure you will see quoted belongs to Modify Video, which needs footage to start from.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5883","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5882","text":"Commercial rights need care too. Luma's terms tie commercial use to whether an output was produced during an active paid subscription term. Check the current plan's commercial-use terms before generating client work; Luma also reserves the right to embed watermarks at its own discretion.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5885","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5884","text":"The catch: the most professional output in the category, in five and ten second pieces, with no sound.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5887","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5886","text":"Best for: teams with a finishing pipeline who care about grade and comp, who work in short pieces, and who handle audio separately anyway.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5889","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5888","text":"5. Kling","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-kling"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5891","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5890","text":"Kling is the best per-shot directing tool available, and Video 3.0 Omni is why. Custom Multi-Shot lets you specify duration, shot size, perspective and camera movement for each shot in a sequence, which is a shot list rather than a prompt. Element binding locks up to three elements, built from a character video or two to four reference images, so a subject holds its shape through a zoom, pan or tilt.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5893","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5892","text":"Its native audio is unusually capable too: five languages, mixed-language performance in one video, Chinese dialects and English accents, and precise referencing of which character is speaking in a multi-character scene.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5895","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5894","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5897","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5896","text":"Custom Multi-Shot gives per-shot control over size, perspective, movement and duration.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5899","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5898","text":"Automatic multi-shot planning for when you want the model to propose coverage.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5901","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5900","text":"Element binding holds up to three bound subjects stable through camera movement.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5903","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5902","text":"Multi-character dialogue with correct speaker attribution in the same pass.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5905","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5904","text":"Kling O1, from December 2025, does natural-language post work with no manual masking or keyframing.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5907","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5906","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5909","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5908","text":"Kling's resolution story needs reading carefully. The standard Video 3.0 and 3.0 Omni modes run at 1080p and 720p, and a separate one-click native 4K mode was added to the 3.0 series in April with separate credit pricing. So 4K is real here, it just isn't what the default credit tiers give you. Shots run 3 to 15 seconds.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5911","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5910","text":"The larger issue is what the terms ask of you. Kling's global service is operated by Kling AI Pte. Ltd. under Singapore law, and its terms require you to label the output interface with the Kling brand, or to prominently indicate that the output was generated by Kling AI where no brand mark carries through. They also bar use for political campaigning, advocacy or lobbying without written consent. For festival and client delivery that labelling expectation is awkward at best. There's also no editorial surface at all.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5913","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5912","text":"The catch: the best shot control, wrapped in the most delivery friction.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5915","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5914","text":"Best for: directors who want genuine blocking control on shots that will be finished and cleared elsewhere.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5917","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5916","text":"6. Moonvalley Marey","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"6-moonvalley-marey"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5919","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5918","text":"Marey puts training-data provenance at the center of its pitch to production teams. Moonvalley's own claim is that it's the first commercially safe video model, trained only on licensed high-resolution footage, with no scraped content and no user submissions.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5921","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5920","text":"The control set is also the most director-shaped in the category: camera control from a single image, motion transfer from a reference video, trajectory control by drawing paths, keyframing between reference images on a timeline, pose control to guide performance timing, shot extension, and reference layers giving separate control per character or object.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5923","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5922","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5925","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5924","text":"Moonvalley emphasizes licensed training data, giving production teams a provenance claim to evaluate alongside delivery requirements.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5927","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5926","text":"Trajectory control by drawing the path a subject or camera takes.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5929","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5928","text":"Motion transfer from reference video, and pose control for performance timing.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5931","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5930","text":"Reference layers, so a character and a prop are directed independently.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5933","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5932","text":"3D-aware scene manipulation, with shots editable after generation including reframing and background change.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5935","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5934","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5937","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5936","text":"Clips are short, and Moonvalley publishes no duration figure anywhere on its own site, which is itself a signal. Its listing with fal, the inference partner it names, offers 5 or 10 seconds with 5 as the default. Output is native 1080p, Marey does not appear on the quality leaderboards at all, and its look is deliberately painterly instead of photoreal, which suits some projects and rules out others.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5939","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5938","text":"The bigger concern is momentum. Moonvalley names no model beyond Marey, and its own blog has published nothing since August 2025. Check that the company is still shipping before you build a production around it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5941","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5940","text":"The catch: licensed training data is a central selling point, but confirm that the product and support meet your production needs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5943","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5942","text":"Best for: commercial and studio work where provenance is a gating requirement rather than a preference.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5945","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5944","text":"7. LTX Studio","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"7-ltx-studio"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5947","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5946","text":"LTX Studio is the one entry with a genuine pre-production surface. You go from script and scene description to a shot sequence with consistent characters, and there's an edit suite attached, not a prompt box and a download folder.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5949","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5948","text":"Underneath it, LTX-2.5 is an open-weights audio-video world model released on 11 August. It generates 4K HDR, and it holds character, environment and voice consistent across cuts in a single multishot pass, which is the specific problem most tools solve badly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5951","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5950","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5953","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5952","text":"Script to shot sequence, so the tool matches how a film is actually planned.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5955","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5954","text":"Native multishot generation holding character, environment and voice across cuts in one pass.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5957","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5956","text":"4K HDR output, which almost nothing else here reaches natively.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5959","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5958","text":"Open weights on Hugging Face with day-one ComfyUI support, so a studio that can't send footage to a cloud can run it locally.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5961","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5960","text":"API pricing varies by resolution and generation tier, so check the current rate for the output your project needs.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5963","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5962","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5965","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5964","text":"Commercial use depends on the plan; an entry-level personal-use tier is not interchangeable with a commercial subscription. The compute-second allowances differ between Lightricks' own surfaces, so confirm what you're buying before committing. The open-weights license also has a revenue threshold; larger organizations need to review the applicable commercial terms.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5967","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5966","text":"It's also a less familiar tool than the others, with a smaller body of craft knowledge around it, so expect to work things out instead of looking them up.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5969","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5968","text":"The catch: the best planning surface, and the least company behind it in the US market.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5971","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5970","text":"Best for: teams who want structure before generation, and studios that need weights on their own hardware.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5973","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5972","text":"8. Adobe","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"8-adobe"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5975","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5974","text":"Adobe is the entry that changed the workflow rather than the model. In September it shipped a generative media tool directly into the Premiere timeline: draw a range on a track, describe what you need, and generate without leaving the application. The model picker includes Adobe's own Firefly alongside partner models from Google Veo, Kling, Runway and Luma.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5977","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5976","text":"That reframes the whole question. For an editor, this is no longer which AI video generator to buy; it's which model to call from the sequence, with the credit cost shown in the taskbar before you commit.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5979","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5978","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5981","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5980","text":"Generation inside the timeline, with sequence settings matched automatically and cost shown before you spend.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5983","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5982","text":"Firefly plus four partner vendors reachable from one interface, so you're not choosing a favorite and living with its weak side.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5985","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5984","text":"Generate Sound Effects lets you use your own voice to guide the rhythm, timing and intensity of the result.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5987","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5986","text":"Firefly's own video model is trained on licensed Adobe Stock and public domain content and never on customer work.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5989","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5988","text":"Firefly Custom Models let a studio train on its own assets so generations conform to a house look.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5991","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5990","text":"Object Masking downloads its models once and then runs against your local GPU, so the tracking work stays on your machine.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5993","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5992","text":"The trade-off","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5995","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5994","text":"Firefly's own video model is well behind the frontier on quality, so the value here is position in the pipeline, not what comes out of the model. Generative Extend is capped at 2 seconds of video. The commercial-safety guarantee covers Firefly only, and the moment you pick Veo, Kling, Runway or Luma from that same timeline you inherit their terms instead, which is easy to forget when the picker makes them look equivalent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5997","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5996","text":"Early hands-on reporting has been mixed on the new audio features: ProVideo Coalition's Scott Simmons found some generated tracks usable and others out of sync and off the mark, and noted that audio designers are watching this with skepticism.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5999","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5998","text":"The catch: the right place to work, not the best thing to generate with.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6001","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6000","text":"Best for: editors already in Premiere, who want the round trip gone and will pick a partner model per shot.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6003","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6002","text":"What still needs a camera","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-still-needs-a-camera"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6005","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6004","text":"None of this replaces a shoot, and the gap isn't where most coverage puts it. It isn't resolution or realism; those are close enough now for a lot of work. It's duration, continuity and performance. Every tool here generates in units of seconds, holds a character imperfectly across cuts, and gives you a performance you selected, not one you directed on the day.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6007","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6006","text":"So the useful reading of this category in 2026 is that it's strongest before and around a shoot and not instead of one: previz and look development, coverage you couldn't afford, plates and elements, extensions, and the shots that exist to be cut against something real. The directors getting the most out of it are treating it as another unit, not as a replacement for the crew.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6009","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6008","text":"Which also means the tool you pick matters less than where it sits in your process. A model you can reach from the canvas you're already working in, or from the sequence you're already cutting, will get used. One that needs its own tab and its own export ritual will not.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6014","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6011","href":"/blog/trim-arrange-export-video","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6010","text":"For the next step, see ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6012","text":"trimming, arranging and exporting video","marks":["b6011"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6013","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6016","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6015","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b6017","items":"$2f:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6022","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6019","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6018","text":"Block out a sequence from one still, run the same shot through Veo, Kling, Wan and Seedance side by side on one canvas, then take the takes that work into your edit. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6020","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b6019"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6021","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b6030","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b6024","href":"/blog/where-to-run-seedance-2-5","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b6027","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b6023","text":"Related reading: ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6025","text":"where to run Seedance 2.5","marks":["b6024"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6026","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6028","text":"one subscription for every AI model","marks":["b6027"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b6029","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}]
32:null
